"""Render the independently verified sharp eleven-qubit sixth-sector minimum."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json,hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;v=json.loads((R/'independent-verification.json').read_text());c=json.loads((R/'value-definition.json').read_text());assert v['globalOptimalityProven']and v['fullPolynomialIdentityVerified']
for name,digest in v['inputSha256'].items():assert hashlib.sha256((R/name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==digest

def eq(t):return '<div class="proof-equation" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'"></div>'
def section(id,title,body):return f'<section class="reference-section" id="{id}"><h2>{title}</h2>{body}</section>'
s='<section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact global optimum · 4 November 2026</p><h1>Eleven qubits:<br><em>the exact minimum of S<sub>6</sub></em></h1><p class="intro-description">The last conjectural sector-length entry is settled by an exact degree-ten sum-of-squares certificate averaged over Kramers mixing.</p></div></section>'
s+=section('theorem','The sharp minimum',eq(r'\boxed{\min_{\psi\in\operatorname{Sym}^{11}(\mathbb C^2),\,\|\psi\|=1}S_6(\psi)=s_\star=113.1090435663466909908720436191490453\ldots}')+'<p>The exact number has algebraic degree eleven. Its <a href="value-definition.json">minimal polynomial and rational isolating interval</a> specify the value independently of its decimal display. The <a href="../algebraic-s6/index.html#n11">analytical Dicke coefficients</a> attain this minimum.</p>')
b='<p>For odd qubit number, define time reversal in the Dicke basis by</p>'+eq(r'\Theta\!\left(\sum_{r=0}^{11}c_r|D_{11}^{(r)}\rangle\right)=\sum_{r=0}^{11}(-1)^r\overline{c_{11-r}}|D_{11}^{(r)}\rangle,\qquad\Theta^2=-I.')
b+='<p>A state and its time-reversed partner are orthogonal. Consequently, the following maps preserve the norm and form a real SU(2) action:</p>'+eq(r'\psi\longmapsto\alpha\psi+\beta\Theta\psi,\qquad|\alpha|^2+|\beta|^2=1.')
b+='<p>Even-weight Pauli observables are time-reversal even. On the Kramers pair spanned by ψ and Θψ, their compressions are scalar: the two diagonal expectations coincide and the off-diagonal matrix element vanishes. Thus every even-sector length, including S₆, is unchanged by this mixing. The verifier also checks the corresponding polynomial invariance directly.</p><p>This real symmetry commutes with physical collective rotations. Averaging a positive Gram expression over it preserves positivity and reduces the invariant space needed to verify the identity.</p>'
s+=section('symmetry','The symmetry that closes the verification gap',b)
b='<p>For unnormalized amplitudes, put</p>'+eq(r'c_r=\sqrt{\binom{11}{r}}x_r,\qquad q=\sum_r\binom{11}{r}|x_r|^2,\qquad P_6=q^2S_6(\psi/\sqrt q).')
b+='<p>The certificate proves the exact polynomial identity</p>'+eq(r'\boxed{q^3(P_6-s_\star q^2)=\int_{SU(2)}\sum_{B,m}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}(g\psi)^\dagger H_B\mathbf v_{B,m}(g\psi)}{\binom{\ell_B}{m}}\,d\mu(g)\ge0.}')
b+='<p>Here g acts by Kramers mixing, μ is normalized Haar measure, and each vector has total polynomial degree five. All Gram matrices are positive definite at the specified real algebraic root. Since the left side equals q⁵(S₆−s⋆), division by q⁵ proves the bound for every nonzero complex symmetric state. The analytical witness gives equality.</p><p>The integral is a finite algebraic operation. Expanding the logical coefficients reduces it to rational Haar moments:</p>'+eq(r'\int|\alpha|^{2a}|\beta|^{2b}\,d\mu=\frac{a!b!}{(a+b+1)!},\qquad a+b=5.')
b+='<p>Terms with unbalanced phases vanish. Exact positive LDL factorizations of the resulting moment matrices turn the average into a finite degree-ten sum of squares.</p>'
s+=section('identity','The global sum-of-squares identity',b)
b='<ol><li><strong>Complete invariant space.</strong> A character count for physical rotations and Kramers mixing gives dimension 1794−1504=290. Direct raising/lowering checks verify the covariants and all transvectant intertwiners.</li><li><strong>Exact zeros.</strong> Every certificate vector vanishes on the full Kramers plane of the analytical witness. The target value and its three independent parameter derivatives vanish exactly in the degree-eleven number field.</li><li><strong>Exact matrix definition.</strong> Each Gram matrix is the identity plus symmetric corrections at 286 specified positions. Those corrections are defined by 286 exact polynomial-evaluation equations. A rigorous interval solve certifies the unique solution.</li><li><strong>Full polynomial identity.</strong> The 286 evaluation functionals and four exact vanishing functionals are injective on the complete 290-dimensional invariant space. A rigorously nonzero determinant proves this. Agreement on these functionals therefore proves equality for every complex state.</li><li><strong>Strict positivity.</strong> Certified Gershgorin bounds prove that every Gram matrix is at least 99/100 times the identity.</li></ol>'+eq(r'286+4=290,\qquad H_B\succeq\frac{99}{100}I.')
b+='<p>The earlier rank deficit arose from checking the unaveraged expression in a larger space. Kramers averaging supplies the missing structural reduction; the proof does not infer an exact identity from a small numerical residual.</p><details><summary>Verification arithmetic and certificate files</summary><p>The proof uses exact rational and algebraic arithmetic, overflow-checked Gaussian-integer polynomial evaluations, and directed-rounding FLINT/Arb intervals. The coefficient root is evaluated at 1024 bits, the polynomial expressions at 256 bits, and the final linear systems at 512 bits. No optimizer or floating-point tolerance assumption is used.</p><p><a href="sos-certificate.json">Exact matrix definition</a> · <a href="covariants.json">Covariant construction</a> · <a href="source-kernels.json">Exact vanishing kernels</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification report and hashes</a></p></details>'
s+=section('verification','Why this is an exact global proof',b)
b='<p>A collectively rotated version of the catalogue representative is</p>'+eq(r'|\psi_\star\rangle=\frac{|D_{11}^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt{165U}|D_{11}^{(3)}\rangle+\sqrt{462}\,T|D_{11}^{(6)}\rangle+\sqrt{55U}\,Z|D_{11}^{(9)}\rangle}{\sqrt Q},')+eq(r'Q=1+165U+462T^2+55UZ^2,\quad T=A^{-1},\quad U=\frac{B^2}{A^2V},\quad Z=B^{-1},')+eq(r'V=\frac{10AB^2-10AB+706B^2+440B+39}{A^2-84AB+1848B+917}.')
b+='<p>The isolated root B≈0.2498461150300332175 and rational recovery A(B) are given in <a href="state-parameters.json">the exact parameter file</a> and the <a href="../algebraic-s6/index.html#n11">analytical construction</a>. Positive square-root branches and normalization are certified.</p><p>There is also an exact continuous family of minimizing states:</p>'+eq(r'|\psi_{\alpha,\beta}\rangle=\alpha|\psi_\star\rangle+\beta\Theta|\psi_\star\rangle,\qquad|\alpha|^2+|\beta|^2=1.')
b+='<p>Every member, and every collective rotation of it, attains s⋆. A complete classification of all equality states is not claimed.</p>'
s+=section('attainment','Analytical witness and a minimizing family',b)
b='<p>Using Python 3.11 and a C compiler, install the pinned <a href="requirements.txt">dependencies</a>, then run:</p><pre>python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt\npython3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>The standalone verifier rebuilds every intermediate in a fresh temporary directory, checks all exact identities, and performs the rigorous matrix solves. The small <a href="arb_helper.c">C accelerator</a> performs only FLINT/Arb arithmetic; its source is included. Expect several minutes and roughly two gigabytes of temporary disk space.</p><p><a href="verify_certificate.py">Standalone verifier</a> · <a href="exact_checks.py">Exact algebraic checks</a> · <a href="check_couplings.py">Exact intertwiner checks</a> · <a href="verify_final.py">Final identity and positivity checks</a> · <a href="pivot-enclosures.json">Certified Gram-correction enclosures</a></p>'
s+=section('reproduce','Reproduce the complete proof',b)
html='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Eleven-qubit S6 exact minimum</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.proof-equation{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.4rem 0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;padding:1rem}main{max-width:1100px}li{margin:1rem 0}details{margin:1.5rem 0}</style></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=11&amp;k=6&amp;mode=min">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav><a href="#theorem">Theorem</a><a href="#identity">Proof</a><a href="#reproduce">Verify</a></nav></header><main>'+s+'</main><footer class="site-footer"><a href="../index.html">All catalogue proofs ↗</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:true,throwOnError:false,trust:false})));</script></body></html>'
(R/'index.html').write_text(html)
